/**
\page page_stfttcollection StFttCollection — FTT Event Data Collection

\section ftt_overview Overview

\ref StFttCollection is the event-level container for all data produced by the
<b>Forward Tracking Telescope (FTT)</b>, a system of small-strip Thin Gap Chambers
(sTGC) that provide forward charged-particle tracking in the STAR experiment
(introduced in the Run 22 era, covering 2.5 < η < 4).

For each event the collection stores three tiers of reconstructed objects:

| Tier | Class | Accessor |
|---|---|---|
| Raw strip hits | \ref StFttRawHit | \ref StFttCollection::rawHits() |
| Strip clusters | \ref StFttCluster | \ref StFttCollection::clusters() |
| Reconstructed space points | \ref StFttPoint | \ref StFttCollection::points() |

A raw hit represents a single fired strip; clusters are groups of adjacent fired
strips; space points are fully reconstructed 3D positions derived from crossing
horizontal and vertical cluster measurements.

\section ftt_ownership Object Ownership

\warning This collection <b>owns</b> every \ref StFttRawHit, \ref StFttCluster, and
\ref StFttPoint it contains.  The internal \c StSPtrVec containers manage memory
automatically.  <b>Do not call \c delete</b> on any pointer retrieved from this
collection.  All objects added via \c add*() <b>must</b> be heap-allocated with
\c new and must not be owned anywhere else.

The collection itself is owned by \ref StEvent, managed by the
\c St_DataSet/StXRefMain framework.  \c StEvent's destructor is a no-op; the
framework performs the final cleanup.

\section ftt_datamembers Data Members

| Type | Name | Description |
|---|---|---|
| \c StSPtrVecFttRawHit | \c mRawHits | All FTT raw strip hits in the event. |
| \c StSPtrVecFttCluster | \c mClusters | All FTT strip clusters in the event. |
| \c StSPtrVecFttPoint | \c mPoints | All FTT reconstructed 3D space points. |

\section ftt_methods Key Methods

| Method | Description |
|---|---|
| \ref StFttCollection::addRawHit "addRawHit(hit)" | Append a raw strip hit. |
| \ref StFttCollection::rawHits "rawHits()" | Reference to the raw-hit vector. |
| \ref StFttCollection::numberOfRawHits "numberOfRawHits()" | Number of raw hits. |
| \ref StFttCollection::addCluster "addCluster(cl)" | Append a strip cluster. |
| \ref StFttCollection::clusters "clusters()" | Reference to the cluster vector. |
| \ref StFttCollection::numberOfClusters "numberOfClusters()" | Number of clusters. |
| \ref StFttCollection::addPoint "addPoint(pt)" | Append a reconstructed space point. |
| \ref StFttCollection::points "points()" | Reference to the point vector. |
| \ref StFttCollection::numberOfPoints "numberOfPoints()" | Number of points. |
| \ref StFttCollection::print "print(option)" | Print summary to standard output. |

\section ftt_example Usage Example

\code{.cpp}
#include "StEvent/StFttCollection.h"
#include "StEvent/StFttRawHit.h"
#include "StEvent/StFttPoint.h"

StFttCollection* fttColl = event->fttCollection();
if (!fttColl) return;

// Iterate over raw strip hits
for (unsigned int i = 0; i < fttColl->numberOfRawHits(); ++i) {
    StFttRawHit* hit = fttColl->rawHits()[i];
    // use hit ...
}

// Iterate over reconstructed space points
for (unsigned int i = 0; i < fttColl->numberOfPoints(); ++i) {
    StFttPoint* pt = fttColl->points()[i];
    // use pt ...
}

// Add a heap-allocated raw hit; ownership transfers to the collection
StFttRawHit* h = new StFttRawHit();
fttColl->addRawHit(h);
\endcode
*/
